{"name":"Uptown Girl","title":"Uptown Girl","revision":185795,"url":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/Uptown_Girl","retrieved":"2026-09-06","license":"CC BY-SA","licenseUrl":"https://www.fandom.com/licensing","language":"en","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Uptown Girl is the counterpart to Downtown Girl. Like its counterpart, it originated from New York City. The aesthetic is focused on being fashionable in a classic way. It features classic and tailored clothes that contrast the baggy jackets and pants of Downtown Girl. In addition, it also includes brighter colors to contrast the beige hues of its counterpart."},{"kind":"heading","text":"Visuals"},{"kind":"list","text":"Pearl necklaces"},{"kind":"list","text":"White stockings"},{"kind":"list","text":"Private school uniforms"},{"kind":"list","text":"Vintage record players"},{"kind":"list","text":"Violins, violas, harps"},{"kind":"list","text":"Chanel"},{"kind":"list","text":"Lip gloss"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Fashion"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Uptown Girl fashion often tends to include the following:"},{"kind":"list","text":"Tailored and well-fitting clothing"},{"kind":"list","text":"Classic dresses"},{"kind":"list","text":"Silk blouses"},{"kind":"list","text":"High heels"},{"kind":"list","text":"Designer fashions with matching accessories"},{"kind":"list","text":"Mature dress style"},{"kind":"list","text":"White stockings"},{"kind":"list","text":"Pearl necklaces"},{"kind":"list","text":"Gold lockets"},{"kind":"list","text":"Babydoll dresses"},{"kind":"list","text":"Frilly socks"},{"kind":"list","text":"Pencil line plaid skirts"},{"kind":"list","text":"Silk hair scarves"},{"kind":"list","text":"Mary Jane heels"},{"kind":"list","text":"Headbands"},{"kind":"list","text":"Lace-tops"},{"kind":"list","text":"Pink bow snow boots"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Activities"},{"kind":"list","text":"Shopping at the mall"},{"kind":"list","text":"Buying makeup"},{"kind":"list","text":"Trying on fashioned designer clothes that look cute"},{"kind":"list","text":"Having fun the city"},{"kind":"list","text":"Frolicking"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Books"},{"kind":"list","text":"Romantic poetry (genre)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Anything by the Brontë Sisters"},{"kind":"list","text":"The Secret History - Donna Tart"},{"kind":"list","text":"My Year of Rest and Relaxation - Otessa"},{"kind":"list","text":"Emily Dickenson poetry"},{"kind":"list","text":"Little Women - Louisa May Alcott"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Music"},{"kind":"list","text":"Billy Joel - Uptown Girl"},{"kind":"list","text":"Paramore - Still Into You"},{"kind":"list","text":"Suzanne Vega - Tom's Diner"},{"kind":"list","text":"Queen - Good Old Fashioned Lover Boy"},{"kind":"list","text":"Lana Del Rey - Brooklyn Baby"},{"kind":"list","text":"Patrick Watson - Je te laisserai des mots"},{"kind":"list","text":"Steve Lacy - Dark Red"},{"kind":"list","text":"Lana Del Rey - Violets For Roses"},{"kind":"list","text":"The Walters - I Love You So"},{"kind":"list","text":"The Weekend, Lana Del Rey - Stargirl Interlude"},{"kind":"list","text":"A&W by Lana Del Rey"},{"kind":"list","text":"Playing Dangerous by Lana Del Rey"},{"kind":"list","text":"Karma by Taylor Swift"}],"contentStatus":"full-source","images":[{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/d/dd/%E2%80%9CUptown_girls_made_me_who_I_am_today_-_%28Uptown_Girls_%E2%80%A2_2003%29.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20230606165352","caption":"“Uptown girls made me who I am today - (Uptown Girls • 2003)","source":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/File:%E2%80%9CUptown_girls_made_me_who_I_am_today_-_%28Uptown_Girls_%E2%80%A2_2003%29.jpg","remote":true,"local":"images/detail/1055-1.webp","localAvailable":true},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/4/4b/It%27s_a_harsh_world.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20230607131033","caption":"Uptown Girl · Visual reference 02","source":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/File:It%27s_a_harsh_world.jpg","remote":true,"local":"i